<title>GERMANY: Daimler jumps to record levels after data.</title>
<headline>Daimler jumps to record levels after data.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Germany's largest industrial company, Daimler-Benz AG, rose to a new record level on Tuesday after Daimler said it expected to report profit of at least two billion marks for 1996.</p>
<p>Daimler was trading at 127.35 marks in IBIS computer trading at 0840 GMT, up 3.75 marks from Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;The preliminary figures surprised the market,&quot; one trader said. &quot;The market was expecting 1.6 billion to 1.8 billion marks,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
